Issue: 708
Evidence: runtime-orientation-shepherd-governed-probe
Worktree: /Volumes/FastWork/adl-worktrees/adl-issue-708-runtime-agent-orientation-resource

Finding addressed:
- The resident Shepherd preload path was oriented, but the later governed
  recovery/readiness probe still sent a raw "Reply with READY." prompt through
  the resident Shepherd executor. That left a production model-facing Runtime
  path where the welcome package did not precede the first task instruction.

Fix:
- Route the governed resident Shepherd probe prompt through
  resident_shepherd_probe_prompt(&orientation), which injects the retained
  per-agent Axioma Polis welcome package before "Reply with READY.".
- Raise the resident Shepherd executor request decode limit for oriented
  prompts so the Runtime can carry the welcome package and task together
  without rejecting the governed probe envelope.

